WEBVTT

00:03.310 --> 00:06.060
m 0 0 l 210 0 l 210 114 l 0 114

00:03.310 --> 00:06.060
Employee Number SP01zs6dg

Designation Product Development
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hDevelopment Group 2
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hPlanning, Team A
Name\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKatase Shiori

00:34.970 --> 00:37.220
<b>Product Development</b>

00:34.970 --> 00:37.220
<b>Group 2</b>

00:39.720 --> 00:42.480
<b>Character Marketing Outline</b>

00:39.720 --> 00:42.480
<b>Group 2, Team A</b>

00:39.720 --> 00:42.480
<b>Shinozaki Takuma</b>

00:42.920 --> 00:44.470
That ought to do it.

00:44.930 --> 00:46.400
Very good, Shinozaki-san!

00:46.400 --> 00:47.730
S-Senpai...

00:49.110 --> 00:50.960
Is your meeting over already?

00:50.960 --> 00:54.110
Yep. It didn't take as long as I thought.

00:54.110 --> 00:58.760
And it looks like you finished 
everything I asked you to do, too.

00:58.760 --> 01:00.620
Excellent work!

01:00.620 --> 01:02.280
Aw, no...

01:02.840 --> 01:06.540
It was just regular work. 
Nothing worth that kind of praise.

01:07.030 --> 01:10.540
Is there something wrong 
with praising regular work?

01:10.880 --> 01:13.220
I actually appreciate it a lot.

01:13.220 --> 01:14.220
Very good!

01:18.600 --> 01:23.310
You know, I really am proud 
of you, Shinozaki-san!

01:25.180 --> 01:29.480
<i>There's a Senpai where I work... 
who is tiny, and cute.</i>

01:42.950 --> 01:47.710
My Tiny Senpai

03:00.950 --> 03:03.950
#01 My Senpai Is Small and Cute

03:03.950 --> 03:06.950
m 0 0 l 180 0 l 180 90 l 0 90

03:03.950 --> 03:06.950
<b>Development Group 2
Planning, Team A
Shinozaki Takuma
(1st Year of Employment)</b>

03:15.340 --> 03:17.930
What're you doing, Senpai?

03:18.840 --> 03:22.570
Sh-Shinozaki-san! Good morning.

03:22.570 --> 03:23.720
Good morning.

03:23.720 --> 03:28.330
It's just, well... 
I saw a cat go into those bushes.

03:24.220 --> 03:31.350
m 0 0 l 180 0 l 180 90 l 0 90

03:24.220 --> 03:31.350
<b>Development Group 2
Planning, Team A
Katase Shiori
(3rd Year of Employment)</b>

03:28.330 --> 03:31.350
I thought it might 
come back out if I called to it...

03:31.660 --> 03:33.560
That's what you were doing?!

03:33.560 --> 03:36.300
It was the cutest thing you ever saw!

03:36.300 --> 03:39.190
A tiny brown kitty, about this big...

03:39.190 --> 03:43.110
Really fluffy and soft!

03:44.690 --> 03:46.200
I already know you are, though.

03:46.800 --> 03:48.580
I was talking about the cat.

03:48.580 --> 03:51.660
Right! Of course! The cat!

03:52.920 --> 03:54.880
Oh, look at the time!

03:55.160 --> 03:56.790
Let's get moving, Shinozaki-san!

03:58.800 --> 04:00.140
R-Right!

04:07.180 --> 04:11.680
m 0 0 l 180 0 l 180 90 l 0 90

04:07.180 --> 04:11.680
<b>Development Group 2
Team A Manager
Akina Chihiro
(5th year of Employment)</b>

04:09.860 --> 04:10.970
Manager.

04:12.160 --> 04:14.910
I sent the plan for our entry 
into the project competition,

04:14.910 --> 04:16.310
so please check it, when you get a chance.

04:16.310 --> 04:20.440
Wait, already? There's still 
a while until the deadline.

04:20.440 --> 04:24.090
I know! But since we'll need to 
incorporate input from the client,

04:24.090 --> 04:27.100
the sooner we get it checked, 
the sooner I can make those adjustments.

04:27.830 --> 04:31.630
Makes sense. Well done, Katase-san. 
I appreciate how timely you are.

04:31.630 --> 04:33.400
Nice one, Senpai.

04:34.080 --> 04:37.840
This is all normal stuff. 
I'm a grown-up, after all!

04:40.460 --> 04:44.970
I have to say, desk work really does 
a number on the back and shoulders...

04:44.970 --> 04:46.990
My whole body feels creaky.

04:47.790 --> 04:50.430
It's even worse when you're 
on the computer all the time.

04:50.430 --> 04:51.720
Definitely...

04:51.720 --> 04:55.350
My shoulders can really seize up on me, too.

04:55.790 --> 04:58.870
<i>I think there might be more to it 
than just work, in that regard...</i>

04:59.600 --> 05:01.860
It's the kind of thing that 
makes you want a massage, huh?

05:01.860 --> 05:04.280
Oh, what a great idea! I'd love that!

05:04.280 --> 05:10.220
<i>Wait... did I just stumble into a mildly 
erotic situation involving a massage?</i>

05:11.580 --> 05:13.150
Want me to rub them?

05:13.150 --> 05:14.500
Would you?

05:18.470 --> 05:23.210
Right there... It feels... so good...!

05:26.280 --> 05:30.220
If you keep that up... I'll...

05:31.010 --> 05:32.140
Something wrong?

05:32.140 --> 05:35.380
N-No, nothing at all!

05:36.140 --> 05:40.650
I get stiff shoulders, too, so I was thinking 
about maybe getting a massage myself.

05:41.900 --> 05:46.160
Sounds like a case where a hardworking 
kohai needs some senpai encouragement!

05:46.160 --> 05:50.090
Aw, come on, I couldn't ask you to do that...

05:50.090 --> 05:51.760
Don't you worry about it.

05:51.760 --> 05:54.540
Just don't fall asleep 
from being too comfy, okay?

05:59.420 --> 06:03.840
Squeezey, squeezey, squeezey, squeezey...

06:03.840 --> 06:06.520
<i>Senpai's tiny hands are all over my shoulders!</i>

06:06.520 --> 06:08.990
<i>I'm getting squeezed! 
She's kneading me like dough!</i>

06:08.990 --> 06:11.430
<i>It's like I'm in the world's 
comfiest theme park!</i>

06:12.340 --> 06:18.750
Shinozaki-san, you're so... hard, and big...

06:18.750 --> 06:23.440
I don't know if my hands 
can make you feel good.

06:24.850 --> 06:28.150
Senpai, uh, I think that's enough!

06:28.700 --> 06:30.700
Did it feel good?

06:30.700 --> 06:33.270
Yes! Maybe a little too good.

06:34.160 --> 06:36.830
Er, forget I said anything! Really!

06:40.500 --> 06:44.440
"And that is my proposal."

06:45.090 --> 06:47.680
Okay, hopefully that should work.

06:47.680 --> 06:49.590
Maybe I should run through it again...

06:50.000 --> 06:53.400
"I'm Shinozaki Takuma 
with Dev Group 2's Team A."

06:53.400 --> 06:56.190
"My proposal involves the upcoming anniversary

06:56.190 --> 06:59.960
of our company's main mascot 
character, Meowtaro, which—"

06:58.470 --> 07:00.170
What's that you've got there?

07:01.020 --> 07:02.430
S-Senpai!

07:02.430 --> 07:04.420
Did I scare you?

07:05.780 --> 07:09.210
The new employee project 
presentations are tomorrow,

07:09.210 --> 07:10.700
so I was practicing during my free time.

07:10.700 --> 07:13.700
That takes me back! 
I remember what it was like.

07:14.130 --> 07:18.670
And so, by arranging a collaboration 
between popular sweets brands

07:18.670 --> 07:20.990
and our company's mascot character, Meowtaro,

07:20.990 --> 07:24.710
I believe we could cultivate customers 
in a new demographic.

07:24.710 --> 07:30.630
<b>Meowtaro Collabo</b>

07:24.710 --> 07:30.630
<b>Currently popular sweets</b>

07:26.690 --> 07:30.300
Er, uh, pardon me...!

07:30.720 --> 07:34.010
I made some goofs 
with the materials for my proposal.

07:34.010 --> 07:38.560
But as you can see, I'm still here, 
so relax and give your best shot!

07:38.560 --> 07:39.980
<i>What a random bit of encouragement!</i>

07:40.920 --> 07:42.710
Thank you, Senpai.

07:43.300 --> 07:48.480
I just have this tendency to get 
super nervous when it's showtime...

07:49.080 --> 07:52.000
They say writing the kanji for "person" in your 
hand and pretending to swallow it helps.

07:52.000 --> 07:53.490
What do you think?

07:53.490 --> 07:55.850
It's probably just a superstition...

07:55.850 --> 07:58.270
Although one theory says the palm 
has certain pressure points,

07:58.270 --> 08:02.560
and by tracing the kanji for "person" 
you can press them for a relaxation effect—

08:00.700 --> 08:02.380
Shinozaki-san!

08:05.000 --> 08:07.090
Something to relax you.

08:07.580 --> 08:10.300
Specially made by your Senpai, 
it's the kanji for "person."

08:10.300 --> 08:12.090
I hope you enjoy it!

08:12.090 --> 08:16.600
<i>S-So close! Senpai's tiny hand 
is right in front of me!</i>

08:17.410 --> 08:20.180
I-It almost seems like a waste to eat it!

08:22.070 --> 08:24.440
I can always make more.

08:24.940 --> 08:26.760
So, by all means, eat up!

08:26.760 --> 08:29.110
<i>She is so wifely, it's killing me!</i>

08:29.670 --> 08:33.110
Th-Then, in that case, don't mind if I do...

08:39.490 --> 08:43.530
Uh, er, did my breath tickle?

08:43.530 --> 08:45.880
Oh, no, it's f-fine!

08:45.880 --> 08:47.250
H-How do you feel?

08:47.770 --> 08:50.090
Better! I think I can do this.

08:50.660 --> 08:52.760
Thank you so much, Senpai.

08:52.760 --> 08:55.790
I'll be looking forward to another 
tomorrow, before my presentation.

08:55.790 --> 08:59.060
Not a problem! I'll be there.

09:02.270 --> 09:04.000
Yamagishi-san.

09:03.770 --> 09:07.270
m 0 0 l 180 0 l 180 90 l 0 90

09:03.770 --> 09:07.270
<b>Development Group 2
Team B, Designer
Yamagishi Aiko
(1st Year of Employment)</b>

09:04.000 --> 09:06.010
Will you be coming to the 
end-of-month drinking party?

09:06.010 --> 09:07.270
Oh, you bet!

09:07.270 --> 09:09.210
That's plus one, then.

09:09.210 --> 09:11.210
You're organizing, Shinozaki-kun?

09:11.210 --> 09:13.780
Yeah, I drew the short stick.

09:14.170 --> 09:17.220
Hey, Hayakawa, you coming to 
the end of month drinking party?

09:17.910 --> 09:20.160
m 0 0 l 180 0 l 180 90 l 0 90

09:17.910 --> 09:20.160
<b>Development Group 2
Team A, Designer
Hayakawa Chinatsu
(1st Year of Employment)</b>

09:20.050 --> 09:20.780
I'll pass.

09:20.780 --> 09:23.800
Again? Sociable as ever, I see.

09:23.800 --> 09:26.620
Quit whining. I attended once, remember?

09:26.620 --> 09:28.760
Yeah, once. The first time.

09:27.600 --> 09:29.660
<i>Stare...</i>

09:28.760 --> 09:30.380
Once is plenty, isn't it?

09:31.550 --> 09:33.300
<i>Staaare...</i>

09:35.880 --> 09:37.550
Are you two going out?

09:37.810 --> 09:38.680
What?!

09:38.680 --> 09:42.060
It's just, Shinozaki-kun seems 
weirdly frank with you, Hayakawa-san.

09:42.060 --> 09:46.040
Th-That's not it! Hayakawa...san 
here is just a childhood friend!

09:46.040 --> 09:49.320
Yeah, exactly! We just grew up near each other!

09:51.320 --> 09:54.780
<i>Dating her? Is that really how it looks?</i>

09:54.780 --> 09:56.180
Shinozaki-san.

09:56.700 --> 09:59.400
Do you and Hayakawa-san get along?

09:59.400 --> 10:00.700
<i>You, too, Senpai?!</i>

10:01.050 --> 10:03.540
It's less that and more...

10:04.370 --> 10:05.900
We were neighbors,

10:05.900 --> 10:09.480
and we attended preschool, 
elementary, and middle school together.

10:09.480 --> 10:13.150
Then we just happened to end up 
working at the same company.

10:13.150 --> 10:15.050
It's kinda like we're cursed.

10:17.030 --> 10:20.300
You seemed to be pretty friendly, though.

10:20.300 --> 10:23.500
<i>Wait, what? Is she jealous?</i>

10:23.500 --> 10:25.850
<i>No, come on, Senpai would never...</i>

10:26.500 --> 10:30.520
It's really nothing special. 
Sure, we chat casually...

10:31.110 --> 10:32.270
I'm jealous.

10:35.540 --> 10:40.480
<i>S-S-Senpai?! She just said she was jealous! 
I did hear that, didn't I?!</i>

10:40.480 --> 10:43.620
<i>And she does seem to be kind of sulky...</i>

10:44.760 --> 10:47.530
<i>Senpai's... jealous?</i>

10:47.990 --> 10:51.670
<i>That'd mean she... about me... for real?</i>

10:53.430 --> 10:55.300
Shinozaki-san.

10:56.630 --> 10:57.960
I...

11:02.150 --> 11:05.680
I... well...

11:09.280 --> 11:13.990
I want to be friends with Hayakawa-san, too.

11:16.570 --> 11:20.000
I've always thought she seems rather neat,

11:20.000 --> 11:23.200
but we've never really had 
a chance to connect outside of work.

11:23.200 --> 11:25.770
If you wouldn't mind, 
could you maybe introduce me...?

11:25.770 --> 11:26.940
<i>That's what she meant?!</i>

11:27.650 --> 11:29.080
What's wrong?

11:30.560 --> 11:33.210
<i>Just regretting my arrogance, that's all.</i>

11:35.250 --> 11:36.510
Welcome!

11:36.510 --> 11:39.120
A party of three? I'll show you to your seats.

11:47.560 --> 11:50.250
Y'know, I tend to attract cats for some reason.

11:50.250 --> 11:51.500
I can tell.

11:52.390 --> 11:55.640
<i>My Tiny Senpai</i>!

11:58.470 --> 12:02.160
This cardboard box is actually pretty heavy.

12:02.160 --> 12:03.990
Let me get that for you, Senpai!

12:04.500 --> 12:06.300
I'm so sorry...

12:06.740 --> 12:09.660
No, no, don't let it bother you.

12:09.660 --> 12:11.960
These kinds of things happen.

12:11.960 --> 12:14.170
Just let me know if you need any more help.

12:14.170 --> 12:15.660
Thank you so much.

12:16.360 --> 12:17.900
Shinozaki-san.

12:18.310 --> 12:19.760
Did something happen?

12:20.260 --> 12:22.900
There was a bit of a mix up with some data...

12:23.780 --> 12:25.760
But it should be fine, now.

12:27.680 --> 12:32.480
<b>40th Anniversary</b>

12:33.830 --> 12:36.710
You never seem to get mad at people, Senpai.

12:37.230 --> 12:38.560
You think so?

12:38.560 --> 12:39.980
I mean, just now...

12:42.040 --> 12:44.620
If someone's already upset 
about their mistakes,

12:44.620 --> 12:46.990
I'm not going to make it worse for them.

12:47.440 --> 12:50.730
Besides, you can scold someone 
without getting mad at them.

12:52.040 --> 12:54.110
More importantly, Shinozaki-san!

12:54.110 --> 12:54.660
Yes?!

12:54.960 --> 12:57.560
You haven't been reporting in enough, lately!

12:58.440 --> 12:59.960
<i>I haven't?!</i>

12:59.960 --> 13:03.090
<i>Did I... screw up with work somehow?</i>

13:03.090 --> 13:04.220
<i>And wait...</i>

13:04.740 --> 13:07.220
<i>Am I getting scolded, right now?</i>

13:07.590 --> 13:10.600
Uh, well... I...

13:11.320 --> 13:15.350
When you work hard, 
I expect you to tell me about it.

13:16.320 --> 13:19.000
J-Just when I work hard?

13:19.000 --> 13:20.110
Exactly!

13:20.490 --> 13:25.110
I don't want to miss your efforts, 
especially when you put your heart into them.

13:27.490 --> 13:30.780
<i>If this is supposed to be discipline, 
then sign me up!</i>

13:32.960 --> 13:34.410
It's a senpai's duty...

13:37.480 --> 13:40.630
to praise a job well done.

13:46.470 --> 13:49.340
Okay, next time I work hard on something...

13:50.100 --> 13:52.850
I'll try to make sure and notice, too.

13:53.670 --> 13:55.220
I appreciate that.

13:58.440 --> 14:02.110
Come on, we're back 
to the office and back to work!

14:03.250 --> 14:05.610
Right! Wait up, Senpai!

14:13.290 --> 14:16.170
<i>It's getting late, 
but I wanna keep going a bit longer...</i>

14:16.820 --> 14:18.870
<i>Let's finish this up, at least.</i>

14:24.260 --> 14:28.410
I bought two by mistake. 
You're welcome to one.

14:28.900 --> 14:30.510
Thanks so much!

14:30.510 --> 14:32.710
Oh, I should pay you...

14:32.710 --> 14:35.390
No, it's fine, don't worry.

14:35.910 --> 14:38.440
I'm forcing something off onto my subordinate.

14:38.440 --> 14:41.630
Think of it as an abuse of authority!

14:41.630 --> 14:44.020
<i>Best abuse of authority ever!</i>

14:44.280 --> 14:47.020
Are you still not finished for today?

14:47.650 --> 14:51.530
Well, I was just trying to 
get to a good place to stop...

14:52.400 --> 14:54.280
I'll help you out!

14:54.280 --> 14:58.040
But, I couldn't ask you to 
trouble yourself, Senpai...

14:58.040 --> 15:01.470
It's a senpai's duty to help a kohai in need!

15:01.470 --> 15:02.420
Besides,

15:02.810 --> 15:05.820
once we're done, I'm going to abuse 
my authority and treat you to dinner!

15:05.820 --> 15:08.800
<i>They made a sequel to 
the best abuse of authority ever!</i>

15:08.800 --> 15:12.170
Th-then I'd appreciate the help.

15:12.170 --> 15:13.300
Sure!

15:14.980 --> 15:18.170
That was faster than I thought!

15:18.170 --> 15:21.310
Only because of you. Thanks again, Senpai.

15:21.720 --> 15:23.810
I'll pay for dinner!

15:23.810 --> 15:26.320
No, not happening. I'm paying.

15:26.320 --> 15:27.560
No, me!

15:27.560 --> 15:28.330
It'll be me.

15:28.330 --> 15:29.050
Me!

15:29.050 --> 15:29.820
Me!

15:31.570 --> 15:34.730
It's still a bit cold at night.

15:34.730 --> 15:37.080
Come on, let's hurry to the restaurant.

15:39.830 --> 15:41.530
Sh-Shinozaki-san?!

15:41.530 --> 15:42.580
Please, just wear it.

15:42.580 --> 15:44.540
B-But...

15:44.540 --> 15:46.320
Put your arms through the sleeves, please.

15:46.320 --> 15:48.270
But I... I'll be fine...

15:48.270 --> 15:49.340
No, you won't.

15:49.660 --> 15:53.340
Y'know, you don't need to have 
authority to abuse your power...

15:56.240 --> 15:59.600
I-I'll keep that in mind.

16:03.480 --> 16:06.790
There should be plenty of places open still.

16:07.500 --> 16:08.460
Okay.

16:09.000 --> 16:12.640
Um, aren't you cold, Shinozaki-san?

16:12.640 --> 16:14.490
Nope. I'm okay.

16:16.410 --> 16:21.020
<i>This jacket he lent me is really warm...</i>

16:21.020 --> 16:25.380
<i>I guess because he was 
just wearing it, but still...</i>

16:25.770 --> 16:29.310
<i>Something about the size and the warmth...</i>

16:29.310 --> 16:32.520
<i>makes it feel like he's hugging me.</i>

16:33.520 --> 16:35.890
Wh-What in the world am I thinking?!

16:36.710 --> 16:38.420
U-um...

16:39.950 --> 16:44.700
I-I don't know... 
if I can continue wearing this...

16:44.700 --> 16:45.940
What happened?!

16:46.280 --> 16:47.800
You can have it back!

16:47.800 --> 16:48.990
But...

16:48.990 --> 16:51.190
W-we're almost at the restaurant, so...

16:51.560 --> 16:53.000
And besides,

16:53.000 --> 16:57.450
we're close to the office... 
What if someone saw?

16:58.070 --> 16:59.180
Good point.

17:00.290 --> 17:03.460
I'm sorry. I should have considered that.

17:03.580 --> 17:06.960
No, no, I appreciate you letting me wear it!

17:07.260 --> 17:09.640
Come on, let's head in.

17:09.640 --> 17:11.460
I'm feeling hungry!

17:13.510 --> 17:14.470
Right.

17:14.470 --> 17:17.470
Odo Eatery

17:16.150 --> 17:17.470
Welcome!

17:17.470 --> 17:20.600
Party of two? I'll show you to your seats.

17:22.850 --> 17:25.600
The jacket smells like Senpai, 
and that's a great smell!

17:25.600 --> 17:27.290
Something wrong?

17:27.290 --> 17:29.610
I-It's nothing!

17:29.610 --> 17:32.170
S-Since it's nice and warm in here,

17:32.720 --> 17:34.980
I think I'll take this off.

17:37.380 --> 17:39.560
What should I order...?

17:39.560 --> 17:43.920
There're so many options, 
I don't know where to start.

17:43.920 --> 17:46.300
You can take your time to decide.

17:47.120 --> 17:49.980
Have you made up your mind, Shinozaki-san?

17:49.980 --> 17:51.630
I think I have, yes.

17:51.630 --> 17:53.760
Then, I better decide, fast!

17:53.760 --> 17:55.800
You can take your time, really!

17:59.350 --> 18:01.640
Okay, I've got it!

18:01.640 --> 18:05.140
Press button for service

18:03.380 --> 18:05.140
I'll be right there!

18:05.970 --> 18:10.570
I'll take the miso-glazed beef tongue 
and mixed vegetable stew dinner.

18:10.570 --> 18:13.630
And a fluffy soy milk pudding for dessert.

18:13.630 --> 18:16.460
I'll have the saikyo-yaki 
cooked mackerel dinner.

18:16.460 --> 18:17.240
That'll be enough.

18:17.240 --> 18:19.000
What about dessert?

18:19.660 --> 18:21.720
Pudding is really good, y'know!

18:21.720 --> 18:26.760
I'm a big fan, it's so soft, and sweet, 
and just plain makes you happy!

18:25.680 --> 18:27.370
I'll take one, too, then.

18:26.760 --> 18:28.920
Pudding, pudding, more pudding!

18:27.370 --> 18:28.920
Understood.

18:28.920 --> 18:30.810
It'll be just a moment.

18:31.720 --> 18:34.970
Senpai, I wanna thank you for your help.

18:35.310 --> 18:36.990
And not just for today.

18:36.990 --> 18:38.050
What other day?

18:41.400 --> 18:46.000
I managed to make it through my project 
proposal without clamming up, thanks to you.

18:46.000 --> 18:47.390
No, no...

18:47.390 --> 18:51.160
It went well because 
you worked hard, Shinozaki-san.

18:51.160 --> 18:53.900
I just helped out a tiny bit!

18:54.300 --> 18:58.650
Besides, I'm obviously going to help 
a kohai who could use it.

18:59.300 --> 19:01.410
Because I'm your senpai!

19:01.920 --> 19:05.500
W-Well, I appreciate all that help!

19:05.500 --> 19:06.790
Certainly.

19:06.790 --> 19:07.660
Although...

19:08.080 --> 19:11.690
Don't try and push yourself 
to work overtime like today, okay?

19:11.690 --> 19:16.170
Working hard is good, 
but overwork is not. Okay?

19:17.960 --> 19:18.910
Right!

19:18.910 --> 19:20.930
Here you are.

19:21.280 --> 19:25.930
Saikyo-yaki cooked mackerel, 
and a miso-glazed beef tongue stew.

19:26.250 --> 19:27.670
Please, enjoy.

19:28.480 --> 19:30.060
Come on, let's eat.

19:30.900 --> 19:33.050
We'll have a nutritious meal,

19:33.050 --> 19:36.440
and then give it our best at work tomorrow!

19:36.780 --> 19:37.690
Right!

19:38.790 --> 19:40.570
Time to eat!

19:41.490 --> 19:42.480
Hot!

19:42.480 --> 19:43.930
Are you okay?

19:43.930 --> 19:45.370
Y-Yeah...

19:45.370 --> 19:47.320
Sensitive to hot food like a cat, too, huh?

19:47.320 --> 19:48.090
What do you mean, "too"?

19:48.090 --> 19:50.580
Oh, never mind me!

20:03.110 --> 20:05.190
Good morning, Senpai.

20:06.600 --> 20:09.640
Good morning, Shinozaki-san.

20:09.640 --> 20:11.350
Calling out to another cat?

20:11.660 --> 20:14.230
Yes, indeed I was!

20:14.840 --> 20:17.730
I heard it meowing a second ago...

20:24.320 --> 20:27.800
Did you hear that?! It answered me!

20:27.800 --> 20:28.830
Sure.

20:30.440 --> 20:35.320
That was deeper than before, though. 
Maybe there's a second cat?

20:40.920 --> 20:44.490
You! You! I can't believe you made fun of me!

20:44.490 --> 20:47.470
S-Sorry! I didn't think 
you'd react like that...

20:47.800 --> 20:51.930
As punishment, for today, 
you have to be kitty Shinozaki!

20:51.930 --> 20:53.900
Kitty Shinozaki...?

20:53.900 --> 20:55.180
I expect you to meow in response!

20:55.180 --> 20:56.560
M... Meow.

20:56.560 --> 20:58.300
Y'know, this might be too much...

20:58.300 --> 20:59.340
Excuse me?

20:59.340 --> 21:00.820
It's kind of embarrassing—

21:00.820 --> 21:02.760
These are orders from your senpai!

21:02.760 --> 21:03.520
Okay...

21:03.520 --> 21:06.380
Do you understand?! You respond with "meow!"

21:05.030 --> 21:06.640
Good morning, Manager.

21:06.640 --> 21:09.260
Oh, good morning, Hayakawa-san.

21:07.140 --> 21:08.120
Meow!

21:09.260 --> 21:11.360
You look happy. Something good happen?

21:11.360 --> 21:15.560
Just glad that my team is getting long!

21:15.560 --> 21:16.290
They are?

21:16.620 --> 21:18.990
All right, Meowzaki, we're going to work!

21:18.990 --> 21:20.630
Right, Senpai!

21:20.630 --> 21:23.060
You're supposed to say "Meow!" Okay?

21:23.060 --> 21:24.870
M-Meow!

21:28.210 --> 21:32.220
Let's give it our best today, Meowzaki!
